SWEET large-surface pixel probe + script thumbnails (patch 0407, oriole Safari 2026-11-19, PixOS doc 57 s.7; LOG ONLY, both default off). (1) Boot-arg sweetsurfprobe=SEC: every SEC s (60 rounds) per surface >= 256x128 (plane 0 of a planar one): non-zero and differ-from-first counts on a 64x64 word grid, a 16-word fingerprint, creator process (new field SweetSurface::creator, set at create), lock/write-unlock counts, last locker and seed; logged on change, <= 48 lines per round (`SWEET SURFPROBE r R: id ...`). Answers whether WebKit drew into its w30r page tiles. Read only (kernelAddress() loads under a retain). (2) sweetscript (patch 0156) takes a 1-number step "T" = the 0403 labelled thumbnail scriptN of the last presented surface (no touch), so a scripted boot can photograph an app N seconds after launching it.
